     "text": "Unlike backup() (RawRRBackup.swift:316-318, which refuses to replace a backup with more beats), the format switch deletes an existing one-shot backup and truncates the points file without comparing beat counts, and rewrites the header captureDate to now; a session id that already has a larger one-shot backup (e.g. a strap fetch saved under an interrupted night's id) is replaced by however many points the incremental caller holds, and the recovered session start moves to the time of the append.",
